<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.7 pct in Sept 1-20-NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.7 pct in Sept 1-20-NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 807 million zlotys, or 0.7 percent, in September 1-20 to 18.18 billion after a 1.7 percent rise in the whole of August, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     SEPT 1-20   AUG     SEPT 95</p>
<p>  change (pct)				0.7	  1.7	 3.5</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   122.43     121.63     90.49</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	22.25	22.09     20.83</p>
<p>  National currency		     100.18	99.54     69.66</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    22.60	23.04     17.18</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    69.68	67.78     49.20</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
